---
import InfoPage from "../layouts/InfoPage.astro";
---
<InfoPage
  title="Licensed briefs for clinics & brands"
  eyebrow="Partnerships · white-label content"
  lede="The same source-linked, evidence-graded briefs we publish daily, licensed for your patients, members, or customers under your own name."
>
  <h2>What's licensed</h2>
  <p>Agewell Brief's daily or weekly feed — one deep read plus two signals, each citing its original source and graded by evidence position (established, emerging, contested, speculative) — delivered under your practice's or brand's name instead of ours. You get the editorial pipeline; your patients or customers never see "Agewell Brief."</p>

  <h2>Who this is for</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Longevity and functional medicine clinics that want patient-facing content without a writer on staff.</li>
    <li>Supplement and wellness brands that want credible, source-linked education alongside their product content.</li>
    <li>Practices that already send a newsletter and want the research synthesis handled.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <p>You receive the feed as formatted copy (email-ready or CMS-ready) on a daily or weekly cadence, rebranded to your name, with your own disclaimers and no Agewell Brief attribution required. Editorial independence stays intact — what runs is decided by the same evidence-first process as our own briefs, not by what a sponsor wants covered.</p>

  <h2>Pricing</h2>
  <p>$99–299 per month depending on cadence (weekly vs. daily) and distribution rights (internal newsletter vs. public-facing site). Priced per account, not per patient — no per-seat fees. Every arrangement starts as a conversation, not a self-serve signup, so the terms fit how you'll actually use it.</p>

  <div class="clinic-callout">
    <p class="eyebrow">Start a conversation</p>
    <a href="mailto:hello@agewellbrief.com?subject=Licensing%20inquiry">hello@agewellbrief.com</a>
    <p class="clinic-callout-note">Tell us your practice or brand, how many patients or subscribers you reach, and daily vs. weekly. We'll reply with a sample and a price for your situation.</p>
  </div>
</InfoPage>

<style>
  .clinic-callout {
    margin: 32px 0 0;
    padding: 22px 24px;
    background: var(--cream);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 16px;
  }
  .clinic-callout .eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 8px;
  }
  .clinic-callout a {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .clinic-callout-note {
    margin: 10px 0 0;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
</style>
